    "done_when": "Read plan artifacts-carry-no-worktree-paths sections 1, 2 and 5 first; section 2 is the specification and this text only restates its measures. At the dispatch base f9940c575 the census `git grep -l -I 'reckon-worktrees' HEAD -- . ':!docs/plans' ':!docs/state' ':!docs/research' ':!*.sh' ':!*.sbatch' ':!*.py'` lists the data files this node rewrites: every non-script census file, under 37 claimed figure topic directories, 33 further claimed directories and 3 individually claimed files. (1) In nova/database/filepath.py add one constant naming the worktree root directory and one public function, relativize_worktree_paths(text), returning (rewritten_text, unmapped_spans) by the section 2 rule, and make repository_relative delegate its worktree case to the same matcher so a path under a removed worktree maps identically. Add the predicate worktree_path_offenders(paths, read) and the exemption constant it applies, as section 2 specifies, with tests; the later guard node calls it and adds nothing beside it. First census the spellings present (section 2 expects only the absolute form under nova-a0f1e0938fc2; only nova worktree paths are mapped, every other worktree path or spelling is reported) and list any spelling the rule cannot map, including a path split across two lines by a line wrap, with file and line in the report. (2) Add a relativize subcommand to the existing filepath click group in nova/database/scripts.py: filepath relativize FILE... applies the function to the named files in place and prints each file changed and each unmapped span; it imports the constant rather than spelling the pattern. The --check mode belongs to the later guard node and is not added here. (3) Apply it to every census file. Leave launch scripts (.sh, .sbatch, .py), anything under docs/plans, docs/state, docs/research, and every PNG and SVG byte-unchanged; no re-render, no solve. Gate, each logged with EXIT=: (a) the census command at head prints nothing. (b) A check script under the run directory re-applies the function to each rewritten file as it stood at the dispatch base, f9940c575 (git show f9940c575:FILE for each rewritten FILE), and asserts the result equals the committed head bytes, and that every rewritten .json still parses. (c) JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_filepath.py passes, with tests for each mapping form, idempotence, the repository_relative delegation on a removed worktree, and an unmapped form returned in the unmapped list with the text unchanged; the tests build the pattern from the constant. Negative control, logged: those tests fail against a scratch copy of the function whose nova mapping is disabled. Every existing test file that imports nova.database.filepath passes with zero added failures against the base; name them and log both arms. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. Report to /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s27/acnwp-rewrite-data-artifacts.md.",
